{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sjbw6rzip5ecs4tuyhjfw7xgmueoiw6tk7qivqjtzj2a52ddktua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and the work found and fixed a real divergence.\n\n## Result\n\n**Configuration surface:** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table and `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no `option()`, so the feature power set is the single empty combination. `check_all_features.sh` derives that mechanically and additionally crosses the Rust `dev`/`release` profiles (release has `panic = \"abort\"` + optimiser) with the C built at `-O0`/`Debug`/`Release`/`RelWithDebInfo`/`MinSizeRel` (built *outside* `c_src/`, selected via `CDIFF_C_SO`). **All 11 configurations pass.**\n\n**Phase A artifacts:** `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (14 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (45 rows).\n\n**Phase D symbol parity:** the C `.so` exports exactly 7 symbols; the `nm -D` diff against the Rust `.so` is **empty** in both debug and release, with 0 non-libc undefined symbols. No module was missing, so nothing had to be translated.\n\n**Tests (71, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s — never a direct Rust call):**\n- `valid_paths.rs` (44) — every `CONFIGS.md` row, randomized with fixed seeds, comparing return values **and** the bytes each library `printf`s (fd-1 `dup2` capture).\n- `error_paths.rs` (18) — every `ERRORS.md` row, incl. NULL pointers, oversized/negative lengths, and out-of-range `mode` ints one step past and far outside the `switch`. The four `malloc`-returns-NULL rows are reached with an `LD_PRELOAD` interposer.\n- `heap_poison.rs` (6), `symbols.rs` (3).\n\n**A real divergence found and fixed.** In the **release** build, LLVM deleted the non-escaping `malloc`/`free` pair inside `copy_and_sum` once it was inlined into `complexmode`'s mode-3 arm. With the allocation gone the `NULL` check was unreachable, so under allocation failure the C printed `Memory allocation failed` and returned `-1` while the Rust returned `21`. `src/lib.rs` now routes all three `malloc()` results through a `black_box` identity so every allocation — and every `NULL` check the C performs — survives at all optimisation levels.\n\nTwo coverage gaps were closed after an independent audit, each validated by mutation testing rather than assumed:\n- **Row 44 (non-zero heap):** the C reads two partially written buffers, so a `strcpy` that drops its NUL is invisible on fresh zero-filled pages — I confirmed such a mutant passes all 44 fresh-heap tests and is caught only here.\n- **Row 45 (malloc request-size log):** a zero- instead of sign-extended `count * sizeof(int)` produces an identical *outcome* (both sizes fail), and I confirmed that mutant survives every other test; the size log catches it, and it was also what first exposed the release-build divergence above.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the fd-1 capture requires single-threaded execution, so `.cargo/config.toml` sets `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` and the harness asserts it rather than failing intermittently. `c_src/` source files are unmodified (only the documented `c_src/build/` output was created)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2047,"cache_read_input_tokens":225290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2047,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f77016da-56db-46ae-8e98-e50f61a4e5bc","uuid":"0de2fd6d-734f-4637-9121-97a8271922ff","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:26:08.062Z"}
